  "findings": [
    "Unsealed action response medians remain about 20 ms across the three levels; this run does not show a monotonic increase in that phase.",
    "Sealed acquisitions and resume planning dominate measured request time. Prefixes acquire unequal numbers of transitions, so raw sealing durations are not directly comparable.",
    "Late single-action graph seals still cost about 1.4 to 1.6 seconds; changing contact state, scene and retained history prevent attributing the difference solely to accumulation.",
    "Canonical serialization/validation and bounded-cache insertion/eviction dominate sampled self time. Some of the same cost belongs to proof-only helper inspection and must be separated from product execution."
  ],
  "nextPriority": "Investigate bounded-cache insertion/eviction and repeated canonical validation/digest traversal on actual sealed-prefix and checkpoint paths. Preserve immutable ownership checks, source digest values, cache bounds and every retained revision. Quantify changes on a fixed retained-public trajectory before claiming a gain; proof inspection is a separate diagnostic cost.",
